 @alvinlepik5265  I guess mostly that he spent a total of 49 seconds talking about both DLSS and RT, which in their eyes are the two prominent features of their GPU development and industry influence. And in those 49 seconds, he falsely claimed that 3080 is faster in stuff like ray tracing [and DLSS], because it's a faster GPU, not because of generational improvements in RT cores. Even though it has better RT performance (48% generational uplift in RT vs 38% uplift in rasterization (calculated from the chart at 23:08)) with the same RT core count , and same DLSS  performance (48% vs ~48.5%) with nearly half the tensor core count. Both points are impressive improvements generation to generation. 

Also, not sure if it counts, but "disappointing 1440p performance difference" is clearly due to a CPU bottleneck. 1080p performance difference is even worse, for exactly the same reason, which is why they didn't even include in the review.

I do however think it's a bit childish of Nvidia to basically blocklist this channel because of that, especially when Hardware Unboxed by far isn't the only major channel doing the same things.

